Email Marketing: Campaign Email Declined from Certain Sender Addresses
Wix does not allow sending email marketing campaigns from certain email domains. We automatically decline any campaign sent from these addresses. If your email address is associated to one of the below domains, update your sender email in order to send future campaigns.Most common declined email addresses:
@mail.com (including all domains used by mail.com services) @email.com @store.com @contact.com @shop.comNote:The above addresses are only the most common examples of declined email addresses. To avoid these errors in the future, do not apply a mailbox you don't own in the sender address.

CMS Request: Limiting the Selection Tags Input Element to One Selection Only
Currently, it is not possible to set the Selection Tags input element to only accept one selection from the list of choices. In this element, visitors can select multiple options from the available choices. WorkaroundUsing Velo, you can limit the Selection Tags input element to only allow visitors to choose one selection at a time. Wix EditorEditor XStudio Editor 
Go to your Editor. Go to the page with the connected Selection Tags element.  Enable Velo Dev Mode: 

Click Dev Mode at the top of the Editor.  Click Turn on Dev Mode.    Replace the gray text with the code below, after the first line: $w.onReady(function () { $w('#selectionTags1').onChange((event) => {
       const indeces = $w('#selectionTags1').selectedIndices;
       const singleIndex = indeces.slice(-1);
       $w('#selectionTags1').selectedIndices = singleIndex
   })
(If needed) Replace selectionTags1 with the ID of your Selection Tags element. Click the relevant Selection Tags element to find its ID in the Properties and Events panel.
Note: Do not remove the hashtag (#) or apostrophes (') in the code.
